@startuml

title Resident Issue Report and Resolution Confirmation Journey

autonumber

actor Resident
actor "Assigned Staff / Triage Team" as Staff
participant "Resident / Staff App" as App
participant "ReportController\n/api/v1/reports" as Controller
participant "ReportServiceImpl" as ReportService
participant "ReportAssignmentServiceImpl" as AssignmentService
participant "StaffRoutingEligibilityChecker" as Eligibility
participant "ReportResolutionNotificationService" as ResolutionNotifications
participant "NotificationService" as NotificationService
database "Application Database" as DB
participant "After-commit listener\nReportAssignmentPushListener" as PushListener

== Resident submits issue ==
Resident -> App : Enter report details\n(community, category, title, description)
App -> Controller : POST /api/v1/reports
Controller -> ReportService : submitReport(request)

group Report submission transaction
    ReportService -> DB : Resolve authenticated resident,\nactive community, membership, category
    DB --> ReportService : Validated records
    ReportService -> DB : Create report (OPEN)
    DB --> ReportService : Saved report
    ReportService -> AssignmentService : assignOnSubmission(report)
    AssignmentService -> DB : Find route by community + category
    DB --> AssignmentService : Route or none

    alt Active route to staff
        AssignmentService -> Eligibility : Validate same-community active eligible staff
        Eligibility -> DB : Check membership, account, role and REPORT_MANAGE
        DB --> Eligibility : Eligible / ineligible
    else PMO route, missing/inactive route, or ineligible staff
        AssignmentService -> AssignmentService : Use PMO_REVIEW_QUEUE fallback
    end

    alt Staff is eligible
        AssignmentService -> DB : Save STAFF assignment\nCATEGORY_ROUTING / ASSIGNED
        AssignmentService -> DB : Save assignment history
        AssignmentService -> NotificationService : Create REPORT_ASSIGNED notification
    else Use PMO Review Queue
        AssignmentService -> DB : Save PMO assignment\nPMO_FALLBACK / AWAITING_TRIAGE
        AssignmentService -> DB : Save assignment history
        AssignmentService -> DB : Find active triage recipients
        loop Each triage recipient
            AssignmentService -> NotificationService : Create REPORT_SUBMITTED notification
        end
    end

    NotificationService -> DB : Persist database notification(s)
    AssignmentService -> AssignmentService : Publish notification event(s)
end

== Submission transaction commits ==
loop Each notification event
    PushListener -> PushListener : After-commit hook
    note right
    No push provider is integrated;
    currently logs event identifiers only.
    end note
end
ReportService --> Controller : ReportResponse with handler and status
Controller --> App : 201 Created
App --> Resident : Show report and assigned handler / PMO queue

== Staff reports work complete ==
Staff -> App : Mark report resolved
App -> Controller : PUT /api/v1/reports/{reportId}\nstatus = RESOLVED
Controller -> ReportService : updateReport(reportId, request)
group Resolution request transaction
    ReportService -> DB : Verify report-management permission\nand save AWAITING_RESIDENT_CONFIRMATION
    ReportService -> ResolutionNotifications : Notify reporting resident
    ResolutionNotifications -> NotificationService : Create REPORT_RESOLVED notification
    NotificationService -> DB : Persist notification
    ResolutionNotifications -> ResolutionNotifications : Publish notification event
end
== Resolution request commits ==
PushListener -> PushListener : Log after-commit event
ReportService --> App : ReportResponse\nstatus = AWAITING_RESIDENT_CONFIRMATION
App --> Resident : Show “Yes, resolved” /\n“No, still an issue”

== Resident decides ==
Resident -> App : Choose resolution decision
App -> Controller : POST /api/v1/reports/{reportId}/resolution-response\nCONFIRMED_RESOLVED or STILL_AN_ISSUE
Controller -> ReportService : respondToResolution(reportId, request)
group Resident decision transaction
    ReportService -> DB : Lock report; verify reporter ownership\nand awaiting-confirmation status
    DB --> ReportService : Report
    alt CONFIRMED_RESOLVED
        ReportService -> DB : Set status CLOSED
        ReportService -> DB : Save resolution decision history
        ReportService -> ResolutionNotifications : Notify assigned handler / triage
    else STILL_AN_ISSUE
        ReportService -> DB : Set status IN_PROGRESS;\nclear resolvedAt; retain current handler
        ReportService -> DB : Save resolution decision history
        ReportService -> ResolutionNotifications : Notify assigned handler / triage
    end
    ResolutionNotifications -> NotificationService : Create decision notification(s)
    NotificationService -> DB : Persist notification(s)
    ResolutionNotifications -> ResolutionNotifications : Publish notification event(s)
end
== Resident decision commits ==
loop Each notification event
    PushListener -> PushListener : Log after-commit event
end
ReportService --> App : Updated ReportResponse
App --> Resident : Show CLOSED or IN_PROGRESS status
App --> Staff : Show resident decision in report status

note over DB
Report creation, assignment, assignment history, notification creation,
and resolution decisions each commit atomically within their transaction.
end note

@enduml
